!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section NO2: NO2 + hv --> NO + O(3P)
! This table has been copied from the crs2004 file
! (no difference between the two versions).
! The reason is that JPL-2006 gives values for two temperatures (T = 220, 294K).
! The only way to use them is to introduce a linear dependence in temperature.
! Since it is already what it was done in the previous version (crs2004),
! the latter was kept instead of using JPL-2006.
! Rem1: Quantum Yield is given below (interpolated from JPL97).
! Rem2: Temperature dependence:
!   i) 185-274nm : T indep.
!  ii) 274-422.5nm : T dep. according to the formula:
!       crs = crs_on_file + ta_no2*T(celsius!)
!      Source : JPL97(tables13&14,p.156-157)
!-------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        52 | Finishes at wl interval :   117
